WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.650
(gentle music)

00:00:01.650 --> 00:00:04.260
Jenna: On this episode of
Travel Dares: Season US,

00:00:04.260 --> 00:00:05.760
I'm digging below the surface

00:00:05.760 --> 00:00:07.740
to learn more about the country's tallest

00:00:07.740 --> 00:00:10.083
and deepest underground waterfall.

00:00:14.672 --> 00:00:16.760
(upbeat music)

00:00:16.760 --> 00:00:18.760
Last episode, I received a clue about

00:00:18.760 --> 00:00:20.490
where I'd end up on this episode.

00:00:20.490 --> 00:00:21.800
You'll have to go underground

00:00:21.800 --> 00:00:24.240
to see this tall beauty in person.

00:00:24.240 --> 00:00:26.100
So now I'm here in Chattanooga

00:00:26.100 --> 00:00:30.170
to go see one of its most
iconic destinations, Ruby Falls.

00:00:30.170 --> 00:00:31.003
As you can see,

00:00:31.003 --> 00:00:33.610
the views are incredible
from the Edwin Hotel,

00:00:33.610 --> 00:00:35.970
looking over at the Walnut Street Bridge.

00:00:35.970 --> 00:00:38.620
While the views are stunning from above,

00:00:38.620 --> 00:00:41.300
I can't wait to learn more
about this Appalachian wonder

00:00:41.300 --> 00:00:43.790
that sits below the surface.

00:00:43.790 --> 00:00:46.420
So this is my first time in Chattanooga.

00:00:46.420 --> 00:00:47.840
I am loving it.

00:00:47.840 --> 00:00:48.960
I have been to a cave.

00:00:48.960 --> 00:00:49.933
I've been to a waterfall,

00:00:49.933 --> 00:00:52.670
but I've never been to
a waterfall in a cave.

00:00:52.670 --> 00:00:55.683
I am so pumped to see
what that is all about.

00:00:57.820 --> 00:00:59.860
- Hi, I'm Grant. I'm gonna
be your tour guide today.

00:00:59.860 --> 00:01:00.693
Jenna: Hi Grant. I'm Jenna.

00:01:00.693 --> 00:01:02.394
Grant: Welcome to Ruby
Falls. Nice to meet you.

00:01:02.394 --> 00:01:03.227
Jenna: Thanks for having me.

00:01:03.227 --> 00:01:04.855
Grant: Our pleasure.
We're excited to have you.

00:01:04.855 --> 00:01:07.660
So right now we are standing
on top of the 80-foot

00:01:07.660 --> 00:01:08.850
Lookout Mountain tower.

00:01:08.850 --> 00:01:11.540
We'll go 260 feet down into the cave,

00:01:11.540 --> 00:01:13.080
and then it's about a half mile walk.

00:01:13.080 --> 00:01:14.370
And by the time we get to the falls,

00:01:14.370 --> 00:01:16.715
we'll be at 1,120 feet under the summit

00:01:16.715 --> 00:01:17.860
of Lookout Mountain.
Jenna: What!

00:01:17.860 --> 00:01:19.326
Grant: Yeah.
Jenna: That's amazing.

00:01:19.326 --> 00:01:20.717
Grant: Ruby Falls is the

00:01:20.717 --> 00:01:22.990
tallest and deepest underground waterfall

00:01:22.990 --> 00:01:24.870
that's open to the public
in the United States.

00:01:24.870 --> 00:01:27.290
And we were discovered by
accident by our founder,

00:01:27.290 --> 00:01:28.888
Leo Lambert in 1928.

00:01:28.888 --> 00:01:31.110
He was actually digging into the mountain

00:01:31.110 --> 00:01:34.100
to find another cave that he
knew about, below Ruby Falls

00:01:34.100 --> 00:01:37.130
and they accidentally ran into
the vein through the mountain

00:01:37.130 --> 00:01:38.470
that led them to Ruby Falls.

00:01:38.470 --> 00:01:40.293
And so it was just kind
of a happy accident.

00:01:40.293 --> 00:01:41.240
Jenna: Yeah, that's a cool thing

00:01:41.240 --> 00:01:42.304
to stumble upon.
Grant: The rest is history.

00:01:42.304 --> 00:01:43.520
Yeah, absolutely. Absolutely.

00:01:43.520 --> 00:01:45.300
And then he named it after
his high school sweetheart,

00:01:45.300 --> 00:01:47.120
Ruby, his wife, who -
Jenna: Oh! That's so sweet.

00:01:47.120 --> 00:01:48.500
Grant: - he followed
from Indiana here. Yeah.

00:01:48.500 --> 00:01:50.110
Jenna: Oh my gosh. I love that.

00:01:50.110 --> 00:01:50.943
Grant: As a matter of fact,

00:01:50.943 --> 00:01:53.610
when Leo Lambert and his crew
first discovered Ruby Falls,

00:01:53.610 --> 00:01:56.030
they actually had to crawl for six hours

00:01:56.030 --> 00:01:57.170
before they got to a point

00:01:57.170 --> 00:01:59.270
where they could even stand up in the cave

00:01:59.270 --> 00:02:01.420
and altogether it took them about 17 hours

00:02:01.420 --> 00:02:02.420
to get there and back.

00:02:02.420 --> 00:02:03.910
So it's much easier for us today,

00:02:03.910 --> 00:02:05.600
only takes about an hour and a half.

00:02:05.600 --> 00:02:07.120
So you're ready to do this?
Jenna: I'm so ready.

00:02:07.120 --> 00:02:08.670
Grant: All right, let's go.
Jenna: OK.

00:02:10.320 --> 00:02:11.153
Grant: All right. Let's go.

00:02:11.153 --> 00:02:13.920
We are now descending at 260 feet deep

00:02:13.920 --> 00:02:15.910
into the heart of Lookout Mountain.

00:02:15.910 --> 00:02:18.470
This rock you see in
front of here is limestone

00:02:18.470 --> 00:02:19.510
and cool thing about that,

00:02:19.510 --> 00:02:22.260
the limestone that was excavated
out of this elevator shaft

00:02:22.260 --> 00:02:24.120
is what was used to
build the cavern castle

00:02:24.120 --> 00:02:25.170
that we were just in.

00:02:26.492 --> 00:02:28.050
Grant: Here ya go
Jenna: Oh, these are for us.

00:02:28.050 --> 00:02:29.500
Grant: Yeah, absolutely. Pick one.

00:02:31.960 --> 00:02:33.740
Jenna: Pretty excited
about getting to wear this.

00:02:33.740 --> 00:02:35.240
Grant: Today's your lucky day.

00:02:35.240 --> 00:02:36.073
Lights on. Ready to go?

00:02:36.073 --> 00:02:39.503
Jenna: Yes.
Grant: All right, let's do it.

00:02:39.503 --> 00:02:41.000
So this whole cave at one point,

00:02:41.000 --> 00:02:42.675
water was flowing through it

00:02:42.675 --> 00:02:44.570
and it's what carved out most of it.

00:02:44.570 --> 00:02:47.280
Now, again, probably about waist down,

00:02:47.280 --> 00:02:49.930
you can see where they
had carved out the path

00:02:49.930 --> 00:02:51.530
so we can walk upright comfortably

00:02:51.530 --> 00:02:53.739
and I'm for one, I'm very
grateful that they did.

00:02:53.739 --> 00:02:54.839
(Jenna laughs)

00:02:59.053 --> 00:03:00.280
Jenna: Oh, what's that?

00:03:00.280 --> 00:03:03.490
Grant: That is our cactus
and candle formation.

00:03:03.490 --> 00:03:05.190
Jenna: I was gonna say
it looks like a cactus.

00:03:05.190 --> 00:03:06.023
Grant: Yeah, yeah.

00:03:06.023 --> 00:03:07.890
So it was basically
formed by water dripping

00:03:07.890 --> 00:03:09.690
through the limestone cap in the ceiling

00:03:09.690 --> 00:03:13.089
and it slowly deposited minerals
here for hundreds of years,

00:03:13.089 --> 00:03:16.450
just very slowly, about a
half inch every hundred years.

00:03:16.450 --> 00:03:17.884
It's also kind of translucent.

00:03:17.884 --> 00:03:19.300
It's made of calcium carbonate

00:03:19.300 --> 00:03:21.307
but if you hold the
flashlight up to it like that.

00:03:21.307 --> 00:03:24.090
Isn't that cool?
Jenna: Oh, wow.

00:03:24.090 --> 00:03:27.680
Kind of reminds me of like
the Himalayan salt lamp.

00:03:27.680 --> 00:03:28.530
Grant: Oh, yeah, yeah.

00:03:31.170 --> 00:03:32.128
So this is beautiful.

00:03:32.128 --> 00:03:34.103
We're coming up on our mirror pool here.

00:03:34.103 --> 00:03:36.810
Our mirror pool is
what's called a rim pool.

00:03:36.810 --> 00:03:38.703
You ever heard of that before?
Jenna: I have not.

00:03:38.703 --> 00:03:41.997
Grant: A rim pool is formed
when constant dripping water

00:03:41.997 --> 00:03:44.122
hits the ground and
pushes away the sediment

00:03:44.122 --> 00:03:44.970
causing a little rim.

00:03:44.970 --> 00:03:46.995
They're really small at
first and when hundreds

00:03:46.995 --> 00:03:50.130
and then thousands of them
just get bigger and bigger,

00:03:50.130 --> 00:03:51.145
they end up forming something

00:03:51.145 --> 00:03:53.053
as large as our mirror pool here.

00:03:53.053 --> 00:03:55.136
Jenna: This is beautiful.

00:03:55.972 --> 00:03:57.480
Grant: All right, well,
we've got a lot more to see

00:03:57.480 --> 00:03:58.404
so let's go.

00:04:00.920 --> 00:04:03.310
So now we're entering the hall of dreams.

00:04:03.310 --> 00:04:05.650
Jenna: Hall of dreams?
Grant: Yeah.

00:04:05.650 --> 00:04:09.780
It's actually a legend that
Ruby, Leo Lambert's wife,

00:04:09.780 --> 00:04:11.570
this was her favorite spot in the cave,

00:04:11.570 --> 00:04:14.070
so much so that she would come down here

00:04:14.070 --> 00:04:16.220
to sketch and daydream.

00:04:16.220 --> 00:04:17.520
If you look directly above you,

00:04:17.520 --> 00:04:20.870
you see all these thousands
of baby stalactites

00:04:20.870 --> 00:04:23.640
that are nicknamed 'soda straws' actually

00:04:23.640 --> 00:04:26.670
because in their infancy they
are hollow in the middle.

00:04:26.670 --> 00:04:29.210
So the waterfall is just ahead. Shall we?

00:04:29.210 --> 00:04:31.001
Jenna: Oh yeah.
Grant: All right.

00:04:31.001 --> 00:04:32.526
(water rushing)

00:04:32.526 --> 00:04:33.688
Jenna: Oh I think I hear it.

00:04:33.688 --> 00:04:36.530
(water rushing)

00:04:36.530 --> 00:04:38.932
Grant: Here it is. Welcome to Ruby Falls.

00:04:38.932 --> 00:04:42.140
Jenna: That is amazing.

00:04:42.140 --> 00:04:43.540
Grant: So, cool thing.

00:04:43.540 --> 00:04:45.134
This room that we're in is
called Solomon's temple -

00:04:45.134 --> 00:04:45.967
Jenna: Yeah.

00:04:45.967 --> 00:04:47.930
Grant: - and it's believed
that the waterfall carved out

00:04:47.930 --> 00:04:49.360
this room started at this end

00:04:49.360 --> 00:04:51.960
and work its way back because
over millions of years

00:04:51.960 --> 00:04:53.350
and they call it Solomon's temple just

00:04:53.350 --> 00:04:55.170
because of its grandeur and beauty.

00:04:55.170 --> 00:04:56.830
Jenna: Yes. Grandeur and beauty.

00:04:56.830 --> 00:04:58.493
This is spectacular.

00:05:00.470 --> 00:05:03.427
Grant: So right now we've
come just under a half mile -

00:05:03.427 --> 00:05:04.290
Jenna: OK.

00:05:04.290 --> 00:05:07.750
Grant: - and we are a
total of 1,120 feet under

00:05:07.750 --> 00:05:09.250
the summit of Lookout Mountain.

00:05:09.250 --> 00:05:13.219
Jenna: Wow. That is breathtaking.

00:05:13.219 --> 00:05:14.061
Grant: Yeah.

00:05:14.061 --> 00:05:16.902
And it's cool to think
that people live up there

00:05:16.902 --> 00:05:18.790
and this is just below their feet.

00:05:18.790 --> 00:05:20.110
Jenna: And they have no idea.
Grant: Yeah.

00:05:20.110 --> 00:05:22.883
Jenna: I had no idea. This is spectacular.

00:05:22.883 --> 00:05:25.270
And it's right here in the US.

00:05:25.270 --> 00:05:27.430
Grant: Yep. Right in our backyard.

00:05:27.430 --> 00:05:30.225
Jenna: What's your favorite
thing about coming down here?

00:05:30.225 --> 00:05:31.833
Grant: My favorite thing is just,

00:05:31.833 --> 00:05:34.460
every time I come down
here, I see something new

00:05:34.460 --> 00:05:36.130
be it in the rock formations

00:05:36.130 --> 00:05:37.541
or just in the look on people's faces.

00:05:37.541 --> 00:05:38.374
Jenna: Yeah.

00:05:38.374 --> 00:05:40.934
Grant: And again, that just
makes the job worth it to me.

00:05:40.934 --> 00:05:43.208
Jenna: Thank you for showing me this -

00:05:43.208 --> 00:05:46.990
Grant: It's been my pleasure
Jenna: - amazing waterfall.

00:05:46.990 --> 00:05:48.568
I gotta ask.
Grant: Yeah?

00:05:48.568 --> 00:05:51.887
Jenna: Before I leave, can I
take one of these home with me?

00:05:51.887 --> 00:05:53.920
Grant: Of course, we have these
for sale in our gift shop.

00:05:53.920 --> 00:05:55.128
Jenna: Yes!
Grant: They're very stylish.

00:05:55.128 --> 00:05:57.440
Jenna: Who knows when
I'm going to come upon

00:05:57.440 --> 00:05:59.702
another waterfall in a cave.

00:05:59.702 --> 00:06:02.285
(upbeat music)

00:06:11.830 --> 00:06:14.590
Jenna: I had such an
amazing time at Ruby Falls

00:06:14.590 --> 00:06:17.220
and to think how long it
took Leo to trek through

00:06:17.220 --> 00:06:18.500
that cave for the first time

00:06:18.500 --> 00:06:21.670
and come across that waterfall?
It's such an incredible

00:06:21.670 --> 00:06:25.310
visual and just gets
my imagination ignited.

00:06:25.310 --> 00:06:28.240
Chattanooga has been incredible,

00:06:28.240 --> 00:06:30.243
but I'm curious where we're going next.

00:06:31.368 --> 00:06:34.980
I think I see a clue that might
point us in that direction,

00:06:34.980 --> 00:06:38.270
time to build music in the city. Hmm.

00:06:38.270 --> 00:06:40.285
I know how to make music.

00:06:40.285 --> 00:06:42.010
I'm not sure what build music means,

00:06:42.010 --> 00:06:45.370
but I am very curious to
find out what it's all about.

00:06:45.370 --> 00:06:46.609
Tune in next time.

00:06:46.609 --> 00:06:49.192
(upbeat music)

